// The regional recoloured rocks - Falador west (Crafting Guild), the Asgarnian Ice Dungeon's
// blurite, Barbarian Village and the Lava Maze runite - and the spent-rock variants they deplete
// into (Corey, 2026-09-29).
//
// Reported in game: "rocks west of fally cant be mined" and "mining - Blurite - only one ore
// works in asgarnia dungeon".
//
// Moved out of content/scripts/_unpack/377/all.loc, following the precedent set by
// rimmington_rocks.loc in this directory: a loc cannot be redeclared while it still exists there
// ("Duplicate config found"). Nothing below is invented - every line is the cache's own, with
// category= and param= corrected.
//
// The cache authors every mine as a grid of (three rock models) x (the ores in that mine), all
// sharing one recol1d - the colour of the rock body, which is what makes a Falador-west rock look
// different from a Rimmington one. recol2d is the ore seam. The last row of every grid is the
// spent rock: same recol1d, but recol2d either absent or equal to recol1d, because a rock with no
// ore colour is a rock with no ore in it. That is how the depleted partner of each live rock
// below was identified, and the model always matches: loc_4027 -> loc_9723, loc_4028 -> loc_9724,
// loc_2110 -> loc_9725 in the 12579 family, and model-for-model in the other three.
//
// What was wrong:
//
//  * Falador west / Crafting Guild mine (recol1d=12579, around 2937-2942, 3276-3290). The nine
//    rocks are gold (loc_11183-5), silver (loc_11186-8) and clay (loc_11189-91). The three clay
//    rocks had no category= at all, so [oploc1,_mining_rock_normal] never ran and the Mine option
//    did nothing. Four of the other six pointed param=next_loc_stage_mining at loc_4027/loc_4028 -
//    "Pile of Rock", plain scenery whose examine text is literally "A pile of lime rock". Mining
//    one turned it into an inert pile that carries no mining_rock_empty and never respawns, so
//    after a few minutes of uptime the mine is a field of rubble. Only loc_11185 and loc_11188
//    (which pointed at rocks1) survived a reset. Their depleted partners, unreferenced until now,
//    are loc_9736, loc_9737 and loc_11165.
//
//  * Asgarnian Ice Dungeon blurite (recol1d=24511, around 3049-3067, 9564-9582). Four blurite
//    rocks are placed; only bluriterock was wired, which is exactly "only one ore works".
//    loc_10583 and loc_10584 are the same rock in the other two models - same recol2d=382 blurite
//    seam - with no category and no params. Depleted partners: loc_10585/6/7. bluriterock itself
//    depleted into rocks2, a generic grey rock that examines as "Stoney!"; it now uses loc_10587,
//    its own model's spent variant, so all three blurite rocks deplete alike.
//
//  * Barbarian Village (recol1d=10500, around 3079-3083, 3420-3422) and the Lava Maze runite
//    rocks (recol1d=4228, 3059-3060, 3884-3885) had the same loc_4027/loc_4028 next-stage bug as
//    Falador west - mine once, then permanent rubble. Depleted partners: loc_11552/3/4 and
//    loc_14832/3.
//
// The mining_table rows in mine.dbrow already listed every one of these locs, so no rock below
// needed an ore assigned to it - they were listed as gold, silver, clay, coal, tin, runite and
// blurite all along, and simply never reached the table because the loc was not wired.

// ---- Falador west / Crafting Guild mine (recol1d=12579) ----

