// ---- West of Falador, between the city's west gate and the Dark Wizards' Tower (recol1d=7329) ----
//
// Thirteen rocks scattered among the trees and dead trees around 2903-2910, 3353-3366, every one
// of them inert: none carried a category=, so [oploc1,_mining_rock_normal] never ran and Mine did
// nothing at all. The same family also supplies the rocks at 2480-2489, 4367-4379.
//
// The 7329 family runs to seven ore rows and only three of them can be named with certainty, from
// colours that mine.dbrow already treats as that ore elsewhere in the same cache: recol2d=6242 is
// iron (Rimmington's loc_9717-9), 13741 is tin (Barbarian Village's loc_11933-5) and 4226 is coal
// (Barbarian Village's loc_11930-2). Those nine locs are wired below. The other four rows -
// recol2d=6346, 14596, 21070 and 23108 - are left alone deliberately: nothing in the build pins
// those colours to an ore, and guessing would put the wrong rock in the wrong mine. That leaves
// recol2d=14596 IS COPPER, identified in game by the owner ("one of the rocks at the west
// falador appears to be copper", 2026-09-30) and consistent with the grid: this family is
// iron, tin, coal and one more, which in a low-level mine is copper. loc_11960-62 are wired
// below. The other three unidentified seams - 6346, 21070 and 23108 - are still left alone.

